 "text": "Home | GCC | Garden City | Dighton | Ulysses, Kansas\n- GCC\nMain\nUtilities\nAbout\nAnnual Meeting\nHistory\nBoard of Directors\nManagement Team\nLocations\nProducts & Services\nGrain\nAgronomy\nAg Tech\nPetroleum\nAdmin\nCredit Applications\nEstate Redemption Application\nFinance Team\nInput Financing\nIT, Process Controls and Comms Teams\nSafety Team\nCareers\nCareers\nCarreras\nInternships\nResources\nMember Application\nCredit Applications\nEstate Redemption Application\nDonations & Sponsorships\nAnnual Meetings & Reports\nScholarships\nGCC App\nNews\nGCC Events\nIndustry News\nExternal Links\nCash Bids\nContact Us\nGrain Elevator Hours\nLocations\nMember Login\nCash Bids\nContact Us\nGrain Elevator Hours\nLocations\nMember Login\nAGRONOMY\nWhen it comes to fertilizer, chemical, seed, and other crop production needs - we’ve got you covered.\nGRAIN\nWith over 30 million bushel storage at 20 locations, learn how our grain department can serve your operation.\nAG TECH\nWith this ever-evolving industry, see what we are doing to keep our growers ahead of the curve.\nPETROLEUM\nOur Petroleum Division is one of the largest distributors of Cenex refined fuels and lubricants in the United States.\nFINANCE\nOur accounting team works closely with all divisions pulling everything together. Forms, employee contact info, donation requests - find these and more here.\nMoving Forward Together\nIn looking at where we are going, there is no way we can not look at where we came from. We came from a group of people who were strong, determined and full of hope. They saw a future through drought, hail and dust storms, and continued to believe that there would be rain.\nMore times than not, they were not disappointed. The rain came, the crops grew and there was strength in the survival. Since it’s founding in 1919, The Garden City Co-op, Inc. has also hoped for the rain, and when it came, celebrated with its member owners, now over 2,000 strong.\nMORE ABOUT US\nNEWS & COMMENTARY\nDon't Let Splits and Units Slow You Down\nOct 16, 2026\n| Garden City\nAs harvest season approaches, take a moment to review your current business units and splits and set up any new fields, sections or landlords. Need a printed list of your active business units? We can provide one to help you review and make any necessary changes. Dig in a little ...\nImportant Considerations Regarding Temporary Changes to Dyed Diesel Regulations\nOct 09, 2026\n| Garden City\nRecent federal action has temporarily changed certain rules and potential penalties surrounding the use of dyed diesel fuel on public roads. While this action may provide short-term flexibility in some situations, important questions remain regarding tax obligations, state-level ...\nFour Locations, One Goal: Local Agronomy Resources for Your Operation\nOct 09, 2026\n| Garden City\nWhen you’re planning around planting, applications and harvest, knowing what’s available at your local GCC agronomy location can save time and keep your operation moving. Meet the local teams and see what your GCC agronomy location can do for your operation.\nIntroducing the New Director of Grain Trading\nOct 05, 2026\n| Garden City\nWe're excited to welcome Donny Huber to GCC as our new Director of Grain Trading. With years of experience in the agriculture industry, Donny brings extensive knowledge of grain merchandising, logistics, and customer service. Please join us in welcoming Donny to the...\nMORE NEWS\nCURRENT GRAIN CASH BIDS\nVIEW CASH BIDS\nDaily Grain Commentary\nRead our daily grain commentary from Stone X\nRead Now\nDaily Energy Commentary\nRead our daily energy commentary from CHS\nRead Now\nU.S. GRAIN MARKET COMMENTARY\nREAD NOW\nGCC WEEKLY MARKET COMMENTARY\nREAD NOW\nFORECAST\nRADAR\nCURRENT\nWeather\nGarden City, KS (67846)\nThree Day Forecast\nSat.\nHi: 65°F°\nLo: 59°F°\nSun.\nHi: 70°F°\nLo: 46°F°\nMon.\nHi: 72°F°\nLo: 49°F°\nZip Code\nGo\nWEATHER DASHBOARD\nWeather\nGarden City, KS (67846)\nWeather\nGarden City, KS (67846)\nConditions |\nSunny |\nTemperature |\n53°F |\nFeels like |\n48°F |\nHumidity |\n37.00 % |\nPressure |\n27.26 pa |\nWind |\n16.79 mph |\nFrom |\nSouth West |\nGO TO FIRST ALERT WEATHER\nGCC E-MAIL NEWSLETTER\nStay up to date with our newsletter.\nSIGN UP NOW\nGCC APP NOW AVAILABLE FOR YOUR SMART PHONE\nClick on the appropriate buttons for Apple or Android device to download. Contact a member of our grain team to create your account.\nInstalling The GCC Mobile App\nFor Google Play\nFor Apple IOS\nAG TECH\nOur department specializes in Agricultural Technology - handling everything Precision Ag related, as well as Decision Ag, and Internet of Things (IoT).\nWe follow Ag trends, ensuring we keep our farmer members as well as our neighboring cooperatives up to date in the ever-evolving changes in technology as a participating FieldReveal dealer and mapping center.\nLEARN MORE\nAbout\nFinance\nProducts & Services\nResources\nNews\nCash Bids\nContact Us\nLocations\nMember Login\nEmployee Team Site\nGARDEN CITY CO-OP, INC.\n106 North 6th St\nGarden City, KS 67846\nP: 620-275-6161\nToll Free: 1-800-794-9389\nPrivacy & Terms of Service\n|\nSite Map\n© 2026 The Garden City Co-op - All rights reserved\nWe use cookies on this site to enhance your user experience. By continuing to use this site, you consent to our cookies.\nOK\nSearch for:\nMinimum 3 character allowed.\n×",
